   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Cylinder and hemisphere",
     "md": "For a cylinder of radius r and height h, and a hemisphere of radius r:",
     "tex": "A_{\\text{cyl}} = 2\\pi r h + 2\\pi r^2 \\qquad V_{\\text{hemi}} = \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3 \\qquad A_{\\text{curved hemi}} = 2\\pi r^2"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Composite solids",
     "md": "Split the solid into simple shapes, compute each volume (or area), then add. Be careful about **faces that are joined**: they are not on the outside. A silo made of a cylinder (r = 3.5 m, h = 8 m) with a hemisphere on top (π = 22/7): V = 22/7 × 3.5² × 8 + 2/3 × 22/7 × 3.5³ = 308 + 89.8 = 397.8 m³."
    },
    {
